Boyun was started as a fork of MiroFish (https://github.com/666ghj/MiroFish),
pinned at upstream commit 7657031ac01184afe2cb220f5ee3545573b5e843. MiroFish is
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3, and its
workflow and architecture precedent informed this product.

The upstream application source that fork carried (the Flask backend, the Vue
frontend and their OASIS/CAMEL and Zep integrations) is not part of this
distribution: it was removed on 2026-10-31 because Boyun never imported or
launched it. What ships here is the Boyun engine, web product, documentation,
whitepaper, tests and NEAR commitment contract, all written in this repository
and released under AGPL-3.0-only.

The full reuse ledger, including which upstream files were studied and what
Boyun does differently, is in https://github.com/Boyun-Protocol/Boyun-core/blob/main/docs/decision-lab/UPSTREAM_REUSE.md. Third-party
assets keep their own notices, including the bundled Manrope font licence and
Boyun-interface/src/boyun_interface/assets/wallet-sdk.js.LEGAL.txt.

This repository contains the Boyun-skills component of the split Boyun distribution.
